## Metadata
Author: Florence A. Reif
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-03-29
Number: 15
Notes: A 13-wide diamond with a diamond-shaped centre panel (r5c7; r6c6-8; r7c5-9; r8c6-8; r9c7, shown as _) printed "No 15"; the intro also calls it "the fifteenth in FUN'S series". Number from the centre panel. Credit as printed: "was sent in by Miss Florence A. Reif of Honesdale, Pa." Intro as printed: "Today's cross work puzzle, the fifteenth in FUN'S series, was sent in by Miss Florence A. Reif of Honesdale, Pa. See if you can solve it. Fill in the little squares in the above diamond with words corresponding to the clews and definitions given below. On another page you will find the solution to last week's cross work puzzle. The solution to today's puzzle will be given in next week's FUN." Four pairs are printed wrong and written here as the grid needs them: "1-1" as 1-2, "31-33" as 31-32, "1-6" as 1-8, "14-23" as 14-22. Read by hand from the Milwaukee Sentinel's page (Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_03_29_86.png), solution from Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_04_05_90.png, by Claude, 2026-11-16.
Numbering: across-first


